==Restrictions==
*This stage uses [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1 deploy costs.

==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 8~10 seconds<sup>240f~300f</sup>.
*4 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'boin]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns.
**2 [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage acts like a culmination of everything you've learned up to this point, as well as a new skill: meatshielding.

Meatshielding is when you rapidly deploy cheap and spammable cats meant to take hits for your bigger attackers, as well as stopping the enemy advance. This is crucial for beating this stage, since if the one horns push to your base, it will die in a matter of seconds.

Spam [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cats]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] to slow the enemy advance, while spamming [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] to deal with the enemies. Whale Cats are decently tanky and can take hits from the Le'Boins, removing the need for Mythical Titan in your lineup.

==Hints==
These hints only appear as defeat messages when losing the stage.
*Deploy Macho Cat and Wall Cat in rapid<br>succession to stop the enemy's advance.<br>This basic tactic is useful anytime!
*Collecting all Treasures from an area<br>will grant special effects! Check out the<br>Treasure list from the menu to see all of<br>the potential effects available to unlock!

